------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Combined-work status — NOT YET DISPOSITIONED
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The terms above govern the sources individually. How they COMBINE in a
distributed image has NOT been ruled. A draft analysis exists for review at
`docs/licensing/m-devbox-combined-work-disposition.md` in the vista-forge
`docs` repo; it is a DRAFT and is not a legal conclusion.

Two points that bear on any distribution, stated here so they are not
discovered late:

  1. AGPL SOURCE OBLIGATION. The image contains AGPL-3.0-or-later software
     (YottaDB) and vista-forge's own AGPL-licensed code. Distributing the image
     carries the corresponding-source obligation for those components toward
     the recipients. Publishing an image while its vista-forge sources remain
     private does not remove that obligation — it has to be satisfied some
     other way.

  2. FILEMAN IS NOT SIMPLY "PUBLIC DOMAIN". An earlier revision of this file
     said it was. Measurement disagreed: 774 of 861 routines are Apache-2.0
     (Medsphere lineage). Apache-2.0 is one-way compatible with AGPL-3.0 — it
     can be combined into an AGPL work, which is the direction this image goes
     — but it carries its own attribution and licence-delivery duties, listed
     above and satisfied by /opt/licenses/.

Publication of the image is gated on that disposition plus the VA
licence-posture check — prerequisites tracker PR-15 / PR-17, in the `docs`
repo. Building and using the image locally is not gated.

Not baked, and why (recorded so the decision is not silently revisited):
`alefragnani.Bookmarks` was evaluated as a companion extension and declares
GPL-3.0, which would add copyleft obligations to the IDE layer for a
convenience feature. It was refused on size grounds first; the license is a
second reason.
